How to Run SmartStock Marketplace
This guide provides the steps to set up and run both the Django backend and the React frontend.

1. Backend (Django)
The backend is located in the smartstock_backend directory.

Prerequisites
Python 3.x
MySQL (ensure it's running and configured in smartstock_backend/settings.py)
Setup & Run
Navigate to the root directory:
powershell
cd c:\Users\Nandan\Smartstock_Marketplace
Activate Virtual Environment:
powershell
.venv\Scripts\activate
(If it doesn't exist, create it with python -m venv .venv and install dependencies with pip install -r requirements.txt)
Navigate to backend directory:
powershell
cd smartstock_backend
Run Migrations (Optional but recommended):
powershell
python manage.py migrate
Start the Server:
powershell
python manage.py runserver
The backend will be available at http://127.0.0.1:8000/.
2. Frontend (React/Vite)
The frontend is located in the frontend directory.

Prerequisites
Node.js and npm
Setup & Run
Navigate to frontend directory:
powershell
cd c:\Users\Nandan\Smartstock_Marketplace\frontend
Install Dependencies:
powershell
npm install
Start the Development Server:
powershell
npm run dev
The frontend will be available at the URL shown in the terminal (usually http://localhost:5173/).
